([PROGRAM 1: Prime Number Generation with Loop Else Clause]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Write an optimized program finding all prime numbers in a user-defined) Tj
T*
(range [start, end]. Use trial division up to sqrt\(n\) and utilize Python's loop else) Tj
T*
(construct to detect primes cleanly without boolean flags.) Tj
T*
(Python Source Code:) Tj
T*
(import math) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(def find_primes\(start, end\):) Tj
T*
(primes = []) Tj
T*
(for num in range\(max\(2, start\), end + 1\):) Tj
T*
(limit = int\(math.isqrt\(num\)\)) Tj
T*
(for divisor in range\(2, limit + 1\):) Tj
T*
(if num % divisor == 0:) Tj
T*
(break  # Composite number detected; abort search) Tj
T*
(else:) Tj
T*
(# Loop completed without break => num is prime!) Tj
T*
(primes.append\(num\)) Tj
T*
(return primes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(results = find_primes\(10, 50\)) Tj
T*
(print\(f'Primes in [10, 50]: {results}'\)) Tj
T*
(print\(f'Total primes found: {len\(results\)}'\)) Tj
T*
ET

